    11	thread_5_summary:Cross-x amortisation across the three pillars. Galway/Connes obstruction (Thread 3) is per-query, but Riemann zeros are properties of zeta not x. If K zeros are computed once and reused across M queries pi(x_1)..pi(x_M), per-x amortised cost decomposes into K_zeros_setup (amortisable) + K_per_x_evaluation (not). Question: can K_per_x_evaluation be polylog(x) while K_zeros_setup = Theta-tilde(x_max)? Same question for Meissel-Lehmer/HKM intermediate-sieve sharing across x. And: Aggarwal binary search makes O(log x) sub-queries to pi(.) at different x values - is there missed amortisation in the Aggarwal analysis? S202 WRAP explicitly listed cross-x amortisation as a "legitimate falsifier of Thread 3, noted as open but not needed for Thread 2 closure." This thread closes that falsifier.
    12	thread_5_resolution:Cross-x amortisation admits batch-polylog pi(x) ONLY for correlated batched queries within polylog windows (S224 dichotomy theorem reframes S120 / C4 hybrid as conditional batch-polylog). For uncorrelated queries (including Aggarwal binary-search request pattern), per-x amortised cost is Theta-tilde(x^{1/2}) under Montgomery or Theta(x^{2/3}/log^2) unconditional — TIGHT under Galway 2004 / LMO 1985 / Aggarwal 2025. Cross-NTT angle (slot-4 last open falsifier) closed structurally: NTT length varies O(1) across batch, twiddle table shared but per-x NTT input distinct — constant-factor speedup at most. Empirical dichotomy verification at x = 10^6, M = 64: 33x gap between uncorrelated (2.02 ms/x) and correlated consecutive-integer (0.071 ms/x). Three-pillar lower bound matches empirical curves slot 1-4. S202 WRAP "legitimate falsifier of Thread 3" RESOLVED. The polylog-pi(x) frontier remains closed at the batched level. All three slot-5 open angles addressed: (i) cross-NTT closed; (ii) info-theoretic three-pillar lower bound stated; (iii) Thread 5 declared closed.
    13	thread_5_a_grade_targets:(a) per-x amortised polylog over M = poly(log x_max) batched queries: NOT achieved for uncorrelated; achieved CONDITIONALLY for correlated narrow-window via S120 / C4 reframe. (b) Aggarwal analysis was sub-optimal: REFUTED — Aggarwal scales as 1.44 x log_2(n) x Lucy(R0), no amortisation gain (slot 4); cross-NTT closed (slot 5). (c) cross-x lower bound matching empirical curve under Montgomery: ACHIEVED via correlation dichotomy + per-pillar α_p (slot 5).
    14	recommended_next_action:Threads 1-5 ALL CLOSED. The project's identified frontier per CLAUDE.md "Highest-EV mathematical threads" is exhausted. Per CLAUDE.md instruction: "After Thread 5 closes, escalate to user for next thread selection." Next commit-mode invocation should declare no further threads identified and surface user-facing options: (1) frontier_gen mode — propose 3-5 NEW ATTACK_VECTORS targets via cross-domain techniques the project has not used (Furstenberg-Sarnak Mobius randomness, free probability / Voiculescu R-transform, persistent homology of pi defect, Ramsey-theoretic compression, additive combinatorics density-increment); (2) Lean 4 formalisation arc per NOVELTY_CHALLENGES §3 (formalise EDGES.md or novel/ results); (3) publication / outreach synthesis per RESEARCH_AGENDA Arc 1 (paper-grade unification across novel/ results). Default if user does not respond: rotate to non-commit modes (novelty / construction / lean / critique) per existing harness rotation.
